 "note": "A routing corpus, which tools/eval_cases.json cannot be. That file asks one request per skill (57 requests, 53 skills) because its job is to prove the skills exist and that the harness routes each one; a router needs the same skill asked for in several ways, because otherwise every held-out request names a skill the training half never saw and no student can beat 'always answer with the commonest skill'. Every label here was read off the live schema in shani_chronoa.tools.TOOLS, and every skill in it declares no required parameter, so a distilled router may also run one without inventing arguments. tests/test_distill.py refuses to train on data of the eval_cases shape and says why.",
